<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Maona of Chios</h1><p class="st-meta">1346 CE – 1566 CE · capital Chios</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Genoese chartered company that ruled Chios for over two centuries and grew rich on the island's unique mastic monopoly.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1346 a Genoese fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simone-vignoso">Simone Vignoso</a>, financed by private shareholders, seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chios">Chios</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and also Old and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-phocaea">New Phocaea</a> on the Anatolian coast. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Genoa</a>, unable to repay the investors, let them govern and exploit the island through a company, the maona, whose members took the shared surname <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giustiniani-family">Giustiniani</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The maona appointed a podesta and council, collected taxes and controlled the export of mastic, a resin produced only in southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chios">Chios</a> and prized as a chewing gum and medicine, as well as alum and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>. The Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> population kept its church and grew prosperous through trade. From the early 15th century the maona paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1566 the Ottoman admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piyale-pasha">Piyale Pasha</a> occupied <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chios">Chios</a> without a fight, ending Genoese rule. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giustiniani-family">Giustiniani</a> were deported, while the mastic villages kept special privileges under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/maona-of-chios.jpg" alt="Maona of Chios" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Genoa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1346 CE – 1566 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chios</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Simone Vignoso</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Genoese Ligurian, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Greece</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Genoese Chios, Mahona of Chios and Phocaea</dd></dl></aside></div>

